A||||8||Formula||Formula vs. 2001 Mustang GT||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||08-20-2001||10:04 PM||||My friend and I we're cruising on the interstate at about 65-70 mph in our "Clique" (Eagle Talon, Pontiac Fiero Formula, Mitsubishi Eclipse, Ford Mustang GT, Ford Mustang Mach1, Honda Accord etc..), and my friend with a stock yellow 2001 Mustang GT pulls up next to me so that we were leading the pack. We were talking all week about whos car will be faster because I recently built a 3.2 Stroker for my Fiero that produced 270 hp @ 7000 rpms at the crank. The Fiero isn't even close to being broken in (250 miles) and the secondaries on the carb arent opening fast enough (running on only 2 bbls right now, 2 of them start to open at full throttle but thats not enough). We both put are transmissions in final gear so we can have a power contest. Mine is third and his is fifth. Next, we count from 3 down and I run about half-3/4 throttle, and he said that he floored it. I pull quickly up to 7 grand (which is way past redline for the old engines tach lol) and gain about 5 car lengths on him. At around 135 mph(guesstimate), he starts walking by me because my engine is revved to the max (so I just hold pace), and he runs up to 140-150mph and flashes the brake lights. I'm happy with this, the fiero can finally hold its own! <P>earlier in the day I beat an old souped up f150 with a 460 (TQ monster). I walked it slowly. and I beat a 3.1 V6 minivan at 1/4 throttle in third. The mustang is the best kill yet.  <P> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||08-20-2001||10:14 PM||||btw.... 3am, and we checked the radar signals for boxes of kittens and school busses full of pregnant nuns.||||reg||1
